785776154923014001-d8bf8108-d918-4d55-9a99-8431095fc807"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ef549fc5289feb9d76eabb6a29f07589547ba38d19c9785bfd7fec104cdd3868","event_uuid":"b15b8f04-c5f0-4fba-bcdc-327cfc493bc3","position":{"commit_sha":"90fd58670cd5e581755ba8803206e085e9c369d3","position":"1785776328176430001-b15b8f04-c5f0-4fba-bcdc-327cfc493bc3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Resolved plan-review finding fa90d8f269a0f5a43 by making the rollout contract explicit: A2-1 dual-writes sidecar and inline stamps, so absent-key GET passes intentionally commit both files; the A1 no-commit regression applies only after initialization on a pass with no absent-key GETs. Also documented every BindingStore.save path, reconcile-check no-save behavior, the git_adapter constant/characterization, and the push.py documentation AC.","timestamp":1785731021418232001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Signed PASS refreshed after P6 remediation. One remaining P6 advisory is intentionally retained: byte-identical bridge-state files plus unchanged HEAD are the content and commit facets of one idempotent no-write contract, exercised by one integration scenario rather than separate deliverables.","timestamp":1785732093968512001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RED oracle confirmed at ecc5c8df6: 7/7 new tests collected, executed (no skip/xfail), and failed for the missing A2-1 behavior. Failures pin max(sidecar,legacy), dual-write persistence, interleaved new/old continuation, corrupt-sidecar repair on the next save, legacy-only migration on save, GET_ROTATION_FILE + push regenerable documentation, the 100..500 extracted-module target with both touched modules <=800, and sidecar-only explicit git commit. Command: pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_get_rotation.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_get_rotation_heldout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_get_rotation_commit_heldout.py. CI gate: make test. Existing test_unchanged_second_pass_preserves_binding_store_bytes_and_head and test_reconcile_check_reconcile_once_writes_nothing are the already-green negative controls and will be rerun after implementation.","timestamp":1785768431731876001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Held-out validation first restored GREEN at 7/7; defect-seeded first-wins mutation (both max seams changed to first-wins) drove the mixed-version test RED, then restoration returned GREEN. Five-axis code review found setup-time sidecar tempfile errors escaped fail-open; a new exact-operation fault test went RED, the same implementer tier corrected it in 1 re-dispatch attempt, and the full oracle is now 8/8 GREEN. Refactoring litmus: tests assert BindingStore behavior, persisted JSON, git HEAD/tree, and clean worktree; only ticket-mandated module/path/size contracts are structurally pinned. Existing atomic-save characterization was updated from the obsolete one-file assumption to assert both durable files and no temp artifacts.","timestamp":1785768929518911001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Full-suite preflight exposed generated docs/env-vars.md source-location drift caused by the A2-1 line shifts in binding_store.py and outbound_differ.py. The generated diff is limited to three recorded line numbers; added docs/env-vars.md to file impact and will amend the regenerated artifact before rerunning the generator check and full gates.","timestamp":1785770634096619001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"A2-1 preflight complete on current origin/main 6baa03046. Generated env registry check, make lint, make typecheck, and commit-ticket verification pass. Full suite on the immediately prior main passed 9433 / 33 skipped / 187 deselected / 1 expected xfail in 32:37. After rebasing the one intervening reconciler change, generator/lint/typecheck remained green and the complete unit+integration reconciler suite passed 2085 with 1 expected xfail. Local review-code is repository-disabled; Gerrit LLM-Review is the applicable review gate. Final commit c5fead4aadbe, Change-Id I6442cb1c3970c2c35ac4f19b0186833a6e785dda.","timestamp":1785773282596556001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed Gerrit change 1295 patchset 1: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1295 (commit c5fead4aadbe, Change-Id I6442cb1c3970c2c35ac4f19b0186833a6e785dda). Awaiting LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments before Submit.","timestamp":1785773310630207001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 1295 merged as e9a25ab84729be0bc9769614f8faa637a1411fac after LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 (GitHub Actions run 30830770038 success), and zero unresolved comments. The current worktree is fast-forwarded to origin/main with the merged commit reachable. Broad preflight: 9433 passed / 33 skipped / 187 deselected / 1 expected xfail; post-rebase reconciler suite 2085 passed / 1 expected xfail; generator, lint, typecheck, and commit-ticket gates pass.","timestamp":1785776130896054001}],"created_at":1785730132111902001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ccef5086-e629-45d3-9ca5-ff52991a6dd8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1841-3a8b-2870-4b6e"}],"description":"## Context\n\nImplement parent story A2-1 as one reviewable vertical slice. `last_get_pass` previously changed up to 20 binding entries per pass even when no real binding changes. Introduce `.bridge_state/get_rotation.json` as the new rotation store while dual-writing the legacy inline field during the rollout window.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Introduce a focused rotation module that owns fail-open sidecar load/save and accessors. Read the chronological `max(sidecar_value, legacy_inline_value)` for each Jira key and write every new stamp to both the sidecar and the legacy inline field. Dual-write is required so an interleaved old binary sees progress made by a new binary; A2-2 removes the legacy write only after its rollout gate.\n- Load legacy-only state into memory. Persist the sidecar only through `BindingStore.save()`; this covers the end-of-pass save plus the write-ahead, recovery, and retirement save paths in `dispatch_one.py` and `binding_store.py`. `reconcile-check` uses `persist=False` and never reaches any save path.\n- Wire `BindingStore` and `outbound_differ` to the shared accessors. Extract the existing outbound wrappers so `outbound_differ.py` remains at or below the locked 800-line cap.\n- Add a `GET_ROTATION_FILE` constant in `git_adapter.py`, characterize it, and include it in the explicit local staging list and basename membership check in `reconcile_helpers.py` so both dual-written files land in one local commit.\n- Update the `_store/push.py` regenerable-files docstring and cover that documentation requirement as an acceptance criterion.\n- Preserve rollback: a reverted reader ignores the sidecar but sees the legacy field advanced by every new-binary pass.\n\n## TDD / Verification\n\nThe behavioral oracle was authored RED-first. The interleaved-binary, real-git staging, and CLI read-only cases were held out from the implementer; only the basic dual-read happy path was exposed. The A1 no-commit regression is asserted only after rotation state is initialized and on a pass with no absent-key GETs. A pass that performs absent-key GETs advances and commits both rotation representations during the compatibility window.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] [code-verifiable] After rotation state is initialized, an idempotent real-repo pass with no absent-key GETs leaves all committed bridge-state files byte-identical and does not advance HEAD. Verified by an integration test in a temporary git repository.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] A pass with at most 20 absent-key GETs advances the same selected Jira-key stamps in `get_rotation.json` and the legacy inline fields. Verified by an integration test.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] The explicit local binding-store commit path stages and commits both changed rotation files without `git add -A`. Verified by a real-git integration test.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] An interleaved old-binary/new-binary pass sequence produces the same rotation order as the all-new sequence. Verified by an integration test that fails if new binaries do not dual-write or if lookup is first-wins rather than `max()`.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] A legacy bindings store containing inline stamps only preserves its rotation order. Verified by a focused unit test.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] A legacy inline-only store materializes equivalent sidecar state on its next persisted save. Verified by a focused unit test.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] `rebar reconcile-check` against a pre-migration store leaves `git status --porcelain` empty. Verified through the real CLI subprocess.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] `rebar reconcile-check` against a pre-migration store does not create `get_rotation.json`. Verified through the real CLI subprocess.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] `git_adapter.GET_ROTATION_FILE` names `.bridge_state/get_rotation.json`. Verified by the existing git-adapter characterization suite.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] The regenerable-files documentation in `_store/push.py` names `get_rotation.json`. Verified by a focused characterization test.\n- [x] [code-verifiable] `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py` remains at or below 800 lines. Verified by the repository module-size gate.\n\n## Files\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py`\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/get_rotation.py`\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py`\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/git_adapter.py`\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py`\n- `src/rebar/_store/push.py`\n- `docs/env-vars.md`\n- focused unit/integration/CLI tests\n\nLanded as Gerrit 1295 / `e9a25ab84729be0bc9769614f8faa637a1411fac`.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"Load, dual-read, dual-write, and persist GET rotation state"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/get_rotation.py","reason":"Own get_rotation.json compatibility and persistence helpers"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py","reason":"Use extracted fail-open rotation helpers without growing the capped module"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/git_adapter.py","reason":"Define the canonical get_rotation.json relative path"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py","reason":"Stage and recognize get_rotation.json in the local commit path"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push.py","reason":"Document the additional regenerable bridge-state file"},{"path":"tests/","reason":"RED-first unit, integration, real-git, CLI read-only, and characterization oracles"},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"Regenerate source-location registry after line shifts in binding_store.py and outbound_differ.py"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","9594-1f1c-bcd1-4774"],["relates_to","1841-3a8b-2870-4b6e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9594-1f1c-bcd1-4774","parent_status_uuid":"375476d0-5a10-4f1d-bdc0-70b3fdc6f54f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["bridge-state","reconciler","rotation"],"ticket_id":"437c-dd9d-9e65-46e7","ticket_type":"task","title":"A2-1 implementation: extract and persist GET-rotation sidecar","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b7161ce7-7854-413a-8eee-b17e661c0d0b","96aa9373-42cf-48d1-a7dd-deba2eeb55a5","85bdeeb5-e9dd-4219-9173-a67643ae833a","d6f210d0-62ff-44b7-9cc0-37828ed89d8b","0e9d5169-4513-49bf-966a-a53db448f095","4ab08e58-f104-4e95-8f07-d8b5515ef21f","654d46ac-43e0-4f06-b315-7ac1a088cda3","5569f22a-140f-4484-ac11-beb4b75558e9","3c8e434e-3ad4-4357-b26f-277ade54ef93","375476d0-5a10-4f1d-bdc0-70b3fdc6f54f","e0030bab-a578-4872-9c6d-b0280a5e1b17","2b2a010c-ab22-466d-9396-b47c42fda52a","2ad2a8b5-3b72-45ba-b048-0daa99a59181","de9969b4-9ed9-47f0-970f-a64a6dddf804","7911661d-5e08-4ff4-b6e4-c491e34d397d","42b8c931-0f35-4497-92c1-400597dc12d9","3dc12219-8fb3-4690-8e8b-54466b581cce","e61c84f0-faba-4623-b5f9-6671e967120a","264ce86c-f286-40fe-b3db-16fc9f2255ce","ccef5086-e629-45d3-9ca5-ff52991a6dd8","0cab2f3f-9e04-486a-8c42-df079c7f835c","d8bf8108-d918-4d55-9a99-8431095fc807","b15b8f04-c5f0-4fba-bcdc-327cfc493bc3"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785776328176430002,"uuid":"2ef53f3a-09d5-4119-88db-3add297b11e5"}